ivative (maybe a corticosteroid?). Indeed, the SMILES resembles a steroid with an acetyloxy group and fluorine. Possibly a corticosteroid like fluocinolone acetonide or similar. Many corticosteroids cross BBB? Actually, corticosteroids like dexamethasone cross BBB to some extent, but some are designed to be brain-penetrant. However, fluorinated corticosteroids like dexamethasone cross BBB. But I need to think.\\n\\nLet\'s examine the structure more closely. I can use describe_high_level_fg_fragments to see functional groups. Might help. Let\'s call that.\\n</think>\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{"name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments", "parameters": {"smiles": "CC(=O)OCC(=O)[C@@]1(O)[C@@H](C)C[C@H]2[C@@H]3CCC4=CC(=O)C=C[C@]4(C)[C@@]3(F)[C@@H](O)C[C@@]21C"}}\\n<|action_end|>\\nenvironment name=<|plugin|>\\n\\n{"result": "Original SMILES: CC(=O)OCC(=O)[C@@]1(O)[C@@H](C)C[C@H]2[C@@H]3CCC4=CC(=O)C=C[C@]4(C)[C@@]3(F)[C@@H](O)C[C@@]21C\\nwith atom ids marked: C[C:1](=[O:2])[O:3][CH2:4][C:5](=[O:6])[C@@:7]1([OH:8])[C@@H:9]([CH3:10])[CH2:11][C@H:12]2[C@@H:13]3[CH2:14][CH2:15][C:16]4=[CH:17][C:18](=[O:19])[CH:20]=[CH:21][C@:22]4([CH3:23])[C@@:24]3([F:25])[C@@H:26]([OH:27])[CH2:28][C@:29]12[CH3:30].\\nThe functional groups inside the molecule are:\\n1. alkene:\\n   Count:2\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: C=C <-> [C:16]=[CH:17] <-> [15*]C([22*])=C[18*],  C=C <-> [CH:20]=[CH:21] <-> [18*]C=C[22*], \\n2. alkyl fluoride:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: F <-> [F:25] <-> [24*]F, \\n3. secondary hydroxyl:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: O <-> [OH:27] <-> [26*]O, \\n4. tertiary hydroxyl:\\n   Count:1\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: O <-> [OH:8] <-> [7*]O, \\n5. ketone:\\n   Count:2\\n   Corresponding fragment SMILES <-> with atom ids <-> with attachment points: 